# N4 (LMX_semantics.ru.md #fields; Codex OPUS-CODEX-20261015-23 Q2: the root heads of the data are its literal heads):
# in D the root heads of y are int: y 0, headed int, and y: 1, headed y -- one place y and one head y, so the bare y
# of S is not ambiguous and S writes D\y: 2. z has two root heads z, so a bare z would be ambiguous, but S does not
# need z and the call runs. Entry 7.
S:
    int: x 5
    int: y 2
end: S
D:
    int: x 1
    int: y 0
    y: 1
    int: z 0
    z: 3
    z: 4
end: D
call: S D
int: r 81
if: D\x = 5 && D\y = 2
    r: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
